<!--Post: 11129--><!--Time: 1110454785-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11129"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bestbud<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bestbud<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 3:39 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Rader and BTK writing analyzed <BR> <BR>Delaina Renfro <BR>KWCH Eyewitness News <BR>Tuesday, March 8, 2005 <BR> <BR>Misspellings. Incorrect verb tenses. Dropped suffixes. They’re grammatical mistakes you&#39;ll find throughout BTK&#39;s letters to the media. One expert says they&#39;re the same kinds of errors in documents written by BTK suspect Dennis Rader while he was Park City&#39;s compliance officer. <BR> <BR>Here&#39;s one example: BTK writes, “I’m sorry this happen to society.” Dennis Rader writes, “She report Walter’s dog running.” In both sentences, the verbs have the wrong tense. <BR> <BR>In 1998, Dennis Rader accused a resident of letting her dog run loose and to prove his case in court, he complied more than 30 documents in his own handwriting and notes he typed about the incident. WSU Professor of English and Linguist, Tina Bennett Kastor, looked at those documents and the 1974 letter BTK wrote about the Otero murders. She noticed a theme of errors. <BR> <BR>“I&#39;m noticing that there are a lot of missing suffixes, plural suffixes and past tense suffixes and so forth.” Said Kastor. <BR> <BR>She saw the same mistakes in Rader’s writing. <BR> <BR>“It&#39;s consistent. Certainly the pattern of errors in these letters is consistent with the errors in these reports. The difference being that this kind of a report &#40;court documents&#41; is a more formal attempt at writing… so you don&#39;t see the same number of errors but you still see some errors of the same type.” <BR> <BR>Kastor says this kind of writing is hard to mimic. <BR> <BR>“Well at one point I thought it&#39;s possible &#40;for BTK&#41; to fake errors- to try to adopt someone else&#39;s voice so that people will think you&#39;re someone else or some other kind of person but that&#39;s very difficult to pull off, and if he&#39;s done the same thing in court documents then probably it&#39;s just he way that he writes.” <BR> <BR>Kastor says the writings also indicate a possible learning disability like dyslexia <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11129-->
<!--Post: 11130--><!--Time: 1110455230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11130"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:crazyhorse4440@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Lola<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lola<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 3:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Great PostBestBud!.....and all the while I was under the impression DR was writing that way to try to fool everyone! How in the world did he make it through college writing like that?? And how did he obtain and keep a professional job, writing like an idiot? <BR>Just my opinion.....maybe someone can enlighten me?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11130-->
<!--Post: 11180--><!--Time: 1110490654-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11180"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 1:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have worked with children with dyslexia, have one of my own, very smart but looks and writes letters backwards. As they get older can memorize the word pattern to spell it correctly, but when in heavy thought 90% of the time misspell or miss read words, which brings up a few other points, First makes sense that all of the Mail Rader sent to Media had return addresses to places he remembered and memorized. Two Maybe he ended up at a wrong address at least once because he transposed the numbers hmmmmmmmmmmmmm.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11180-->
<!--Post: 11188--><!--Time: 1110493988-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11188"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 2:33 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->According to a report in the LA Times, a nieghbor woman of his went to court to fight his tickets that he had issued her dog in 1998. The report he wrote was filled with gramatical errors including switching tenses midsentence.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11188-->
<!--Post: 11191--><!--Time: 1110494230-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11191"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Foxfire<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Foxfire<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 2:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I had a friend at work who had the same problem.  She was dyslexic and the tenses looked to her to be correct.  She was SAYING it correctly but typing it wrong.  So she would end up running a long letter by me to proofread because even after spellcheck, it would not find the incorrect tenses.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11191-->
<!--Post: 11192--><!--Time: 1110494542-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11192"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 2:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey Johno good point and I hear that on everyone of his cases he wrote mounds of paperwork, because he said, he didn&#39;t like to loose, I bet they were the same way filled with errors, unless he had the sense to use the spell checker, but even that brings up the wrong words sometimes.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11192-->
<!--Post: 11217--><!--Time: 1110507068-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11217"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rocky<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rocky<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 6:11 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Ok, that&#39;s a form of obsessive complusiveness fueled by his frustration with dyslexia. Don&#39;t tell me he murdered people because of his frustration with being dyslexic!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11217-->
<!--Post: 11238--><!--Time: 1110520913-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11238"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:embersageblue@aol.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Embersage<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Embersage<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 10, 2005 - 10:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->lol no rocky, I tend to doubt that it had anything to do with him being a sociopath<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11238-->
<!--Post: 11252--><!--Time: 1110529781-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11252"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 12:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Based on hours of intense study, and seconds of studying his &#34;secret symbol&#34; I have arrived at the conclusion that his father would not allow his mother to breast feed him, causing him to resent his father who made him cut the grass later in life, leading to a compulsive need for well trimed lawns, and noticing that men usually mowed the lawn,Became convinced that women were not neat enough. This lack of respect for lawn grooming and at the same time transferring his hatred of his father to women, confused by the breast feeding issue, caused him to take out his anger on women, eventually leading to murder. Whereas if he had just killed his father in the first place he probably would have turned out normal.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11252-->
<!--Post: 11255--><!--Time: 1110531912-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11255"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Superbike7<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Superbike7<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->8-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 1:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have the same problem especially with numbers I get it exactly right  but backwards. Also I have had symptoms of manic depression and when manic your thoughts are racing quicker than you can write and you leave out alot of small words like ing, and ,the,an etc.When talking to people like this they will talk fast and high pitched and dart from one subject to another and back, its hard to follow this train of thought. I have read that people who talk fast and think this way show a sign of intelligence, also people who talk in a high tense voice are often victims of sexual abuse as told by Lilian Glass Phd in her book I know what you are thinking. I have noticed a high tense tone in the way Dennis Rader speaks I would not be surprised if he is diagnosed with manic depression and was a victim of abuse when he was young.Still no excuse for what he has done though.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11255-->
<!--Post: 11344--><!--Time: 1110598995-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11344"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dpinva<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dpinva<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, March 11, 2005 - 7:43 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I agree that it is important to understand why BTK did what he did, but that understanding cannot in <i>any way excuse what he did</i>. There IS no excuse for what he did, however much we understand about him eventually. Period.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11344-->
<!--Post: 11381--><!--Time: 1110646612-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST11381"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Teardrop<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Teardrop<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, March 12, 2005 - 8:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How did he get through high school and college with that kind of spelling and sentence construction? &#40;Which also proves that the pilfered the &#39;Oh, Anna&#39; poem&#41;. When I tested students in the public schools, I found that the average student was functioning 4 years below grade level. The honor society students were only 2 years below grade level: hence the honors.  <BR> <BR>For what are those tax monies going? Sprts? Itz ridickalas!! <BR> <BR>If his defense is worth a nickel, they will have him examined by a neuropsychologist and given a good  battery of tests. They will some up with some kind of impairment. Auditory or visual sequencing/memory, aphasia, etc: Brain insult of some kind. It happens all the time, but we are not all serial killers. <BR> <BR>I think that his candidacy rejection by WPD was the last straw rejection, and he has been making fools of them ever since. Until oops, the computer diskette. Or it could have been the lack of breast feeding!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 11381-->
